nodecode-screenrig is a rewrite of screenrig's screenrig/plugin:

  https://github.com/screenrig/plugin
  commit 37de9fcb22bd1e7e13f881643ac2328b325cb75b

Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 ScreenRig (LICENSE)

The original is a portable agent plugin: a plugin manifest, the screenrig
skill and its references, a second skill for hosted views, an MCP server
declaration for https://api.screenrig.ai/mcp, and screenRIG's bundled Node
CLI (cli/dist, a command surface of well over a hundred commands). This
rewrite keeps the part of that a model reaches without Node: the control API
the CLI is a client of, at https://api.screenrig.ai/api — the screen list and
one screen, the playlist list, the media list, and the one write that puts a
playlist on a screen (PATCH /api/screens/{id}). The section, the bearer
token, the cursor-paged list reads with next_cursor and the API's problem
document are the CLI's own; the code is Common Lisp, through nlk:http.

Left out, and why: the CLI's upload and pairing commands, playlist authoring,
sources, applications and advertising all stay in the CLI and the dashboard —
each is a large workflow with local files, ffmpeg and multipart uploads, and
none of them is needed to answer what the screens are and what they play;
the hosted MCP views need an MCP Apps host to render cards, which a tool
answer is not; and the skill's freshness bootstrap, the plugin install step
and the `docs` commands exist only for the plugin's own distribution. The
screenrig skill's rules that still hold (an id from the list first, names are
data, a pending review waits, a write changes a screen in the world) are this
cell's (help :screenrig) primer.

Nothing of the original runs here: no Node, no CLI, no bundled file.
